    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="15">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 15</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="15" corresp="#wit-hk">E si aucuns est apeled de mustier fruissir u de chambre, e il n'ait esté en ariere blasmé, s'en escundisse par XIIII humes leals numez sei duzime main.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk">And if anyone is accused of breaking into a church or a treasury, and has no previous convictions against him, he shall clear himself of the charge with 11 compurgators found among 14 qualified men nominated [by the court].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="503"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_14-1">Leis Wl 14.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. 14, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_14-1">Leis Wl 14.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 260–261 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
